5.4 Imbalance Method Comparison

This section compares the performance of the seven imbalance treatment methods across all classifiers and both datasets. The purpose is to determine which resampling or weighting strategy provides the strongest improvement in minority-class detection and whether certain methods are more universally effective than others. Since imbalanced classification often requires a trade-off between recall and precision, the comparison emphasises F1-score, recall and PR-AUC alongside MCC, as these metrics are particularly informative for evaluating phishing detection systems.

Table 5.4 presents the mean performance of each imbalance method aggregated across all three classifiers and both datasets. This aggregation reveals the overall tendency of each balancing strategy rather than its performance with any single classifier. Methods that perform consistently well across classifiers and datasets are more likely to be useful in practical settings where the optimal classifier may not be known in advance.

